1. Requirements 5min
  -functional: "users can create short link" / "opening it redirects"
  -non functional: how big, how fast, what must never go wrong. what's out of scope


2. Rough numbers  2-3min
    numbers that changes the design - Requests per second, reads VS writes, storage.


3. API   3-5min
   One Endpoint per feature. accepts and returns


4. Data model   3-5min
  -Main tables and key columns.
  -which database and why
  -index for main queries


5.High level design   10min
  draw components (client,servers,dbs, anything else)
  walk one request through them for each feature


6.Deep Dive 10-15min
  Name the problem, compare 2 options, choose one, explain why


7. Wrap-up 2min
    Recap, name weak spots, say what i can improve with more time

Rules: 
Simple first, then improve (like brute force solution)
Give reason for every choice 
Use numbers to make decisions

What they score on:
  1. pin down the problem
  2. design works end to end, 
  3. justify trade offs and go deep
  4. clear explanations 
